# HiveArmor — Global Rules for frontend-v3

## Product Identity
- Name: **HiveArmor** — one word, capital H, capital A. Never "Hive Armor" or "HIVEARMOR".
- Active UI: `frontend-v3/` only. Never touch `frontend-v2/` or `frontend/`.
- Component prefix: `Ha` for all PatternFly wrappers.
- Repo root: `/Users/encryptshell/GIT/UTMStack-11/`

## Hard Rules — Never Break
- No `any` TypeScript types. Use `unknown` + type guard if shape is truly unknown.
- No hardcoded hex colors in component files. Use CSS custom properties only.
- No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with user content.
- No raw customer data (IPs, hostnames, log payloads) in `console.log`.
- JWT stored only at `localStorage["hivearmor_auth_token"]` — never in React state or URL params.
- All API calls go through the Vite proxy `/api/*` — never absolute backend URLs.
- Do not persist alert/incident content to `localStorage` — only UI preferences.
- No library not already in `package.json` without explicit approval.

## Test File Rule — CRITICAL
Every `.test.tsx` / `.test.ts` you create MUST use Vitest. The project runs Vitest, NOT Node's built-in test runner.

```typescript
// ✅ ALWAYS use this
import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest';

// ❌ NEVER use — Vitest will report "No test suite found"
// import { describe, it } from 'node:test';
// import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
```

Use `expect(value).toBe(true)` and `expect(value).toBeFalsy()` — never `assert.ok()`.

